From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: camss: add SM8150 support

SM8150 is the same Titan generation as SDM845 and uses the same blocks: the
3ph 1.0 CSIPHY, the gen2 CSID and the 17x VFE. It differs by having four
CSIPHYs rather than three.

Add resource tables for four CSIPHYs, two CSIDs and two VFEs, modelled on
SDM845 whose clock names, rates and power domains carry over unchanged. The
lite CSID and VFE instances the SoC also has are deliberately left out of
this first step; the full instances are what a sensor needs to stream.

Reuse the CAMSS_845 version, as SDM670 already does, because the hardware
behaviours selected by it in the CSIPHY and VFE code are the ones this SoC
needs.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
